# The Cyclops wants the lunch first and the water second, in that
# order and without much delay in between -- give him only the food
# and he starts eyeing the player as an alternative drink. Water
# right after settles him, and he falls asleep and clears the stairs.

gib brot zu zyklop
gib wasser zu zyklop
rauf

# Bursting in on the thief's lair through the stairs (an entrance he
# doesn't expect) draws an immediate knife hit -- expected, not a
# sign of a misstep. Handing over the egg right away is what matters:
# he's disarmed by the gift and stops to admire it rather than press
# the attack, which is the whole point of carrying it this far
# instead of just letting him steal it -- a stolen egg stays shut
# and unopenable; a given one, he opens for you.

gib ei zu dieb

# First attempt, with the sword. Costs nothing for a few exchanges,
# lands one real hit, then the sword goes flying and doesn't come
# back -- stolen outright rather than dropped, it turns out.

