# Everything he was ever carrying or had stolen falls out at once --
# coins, the sword, his own stiletto, the painting, and the egg,
# opened, its canary confirmed intact. The room's own chalice is now
# safe to take too, and "nimm alles" gets all of it in one go except
# the painting, which the carry limit only makes room for once the
# two spare weapons (no longer needed) go back down. Dropping the
# attic knife by its full description fails -- "außenhendes" alone
# isn't in the dictionary the same way the noun is -- so "messer" on
# its own is what actually works.

